# ============================================================
#  THE HOLLOW STAR, v2, Act III: escalation (docs/plots/hollowstar-v2.md).
#  New cards; the act's older ones keep their ids where they were (chain_hollowstar*.grim).
#    hs_shadow_late   your shadow moves a moment late (it opens the way to Seraphine's second shadow)
#    hs_grey_daylight the climax: the man in grey strikes in daylight, for the key or for Kael
#    hs_key_recover   the key taken, and four ways to win it back, only one of them a check you might lose badly
# ============================================================

@event hs_shadow_late
title: A Moment Late
thread: hs_escalation
class: story
tone: eerie
time: evening night
weight: 14
art: lantern
tags: mystery hollowstar
scene: A student on a lamplit staircase looking at their own shadow on the wall, which is still raising its hand after theirs has dropped.
text: On the stairs by lamplight you wave to a friend and drop your hand, and your shadow on the wall goes on waving a moment longer. Then it lowers its hand, slowly, as if it had only just noticed you were watching. You stand on the stair for a long time. It doesn't move again. Neither do you.
> left: Find Seraphine, now
  meet seraphine
  rel seraphine +small
  mood -small
  say: She opens her door before you knock, already in her coat. "Yours too," she says. "I painted it last winter. I didn't know whose it was." She won't show you the painting. She does walk you back to your room and makes you leave the lamp lit.
> right: Blow the lamp out
  mood -tiny
  health -tiny
  say: In the dark there are no shadows, and you go up to bed without looking at the walls. You sleep badly. In the morning the frost on your window has melted in the shape of a hand, on the inside of the glass.

@event hs_grey_daylight
title: In Broad Daylight
beat: 8
slot: noon
type: menu
when: met(kael) and since(hs_dark_tower) >= 2
thread: hs_escalation
class: story
tone: tense
art: mask
tags: mystery hollowstar danger
# Act III's climax (v2): two of the act's finds bring it early (hs_escalation_progress), the deadline otherwise; it
# opens Act IV. He comes for the star key if you hold it, else for Kael. Losing the key is recoverable, with or without
# a fight (hs_key_recover; the headmistress's summons).
scene: A sunlit courtyard at noon gone silent and frozen, students pressed against the walls, a tall man in grey walking straight across it toward one student.
on_show:
  advance hollowstar to 10
text: Noon, the courtyard full, and the man in grey walks in through the gate as if he had an appointment. The fountain freezes, then the flagstones, then the air. Students scramble back against the walls. He stops in front of you. {flag(star_key): "The key," he says pleasantly, holding out a gloved hand. "It was never yours."|"Where is Kael Dumont?" he says pleasantly. "His mother would like a word."}
> fight: Draw on him, here
  hint: Combat, in front of everyone. Lose, and he takes what he came for.
  if flag(kael_ally):
    challenge combat expert drift mid with kael:
      win:
        flag grey_beaten
        renown +medium
        alignment +tiny
        say: Kael's frost and your spell hit him together, and the man in grey goes skidding back across the ice he made. For the first time he looks surprised. He straightens his coat, bows to the whole courtyard, and walks out of the gate. Then the cheering starts.
      lose:
        if flag(star_key):
          unflag star_key
          flag key_taken
        else:
          gain grey_watching
        renown -tiny
        say: It goes on for a long minute, in front of everyone, and then your last spell is still in the air when the flagstones come up to meet you both. {flag(key_taken): When you get up, the key is gone from your pocket, and so is he.|When you get up he is gone, and Kael is bleeding from a cut over his eye that frosts over as you watch.}
  else:
    challenge combat expert drift mid:
      win:
        flag grey_beaten
        renown +medium
        alignment +tiny
        say: Your spell catches him square and he goes skidding back across the ice he made. For the first time he looks surprised. He straightens his coat, bows to the whole courtyard, and walks out of the gate. Then the cheering starts.
      lose:
        if flag(star_key):
          unflag star_key
          flag key_taken
        else:
          gain grey_watching
        renown -tiny
        say: You trade spells with him across the frozen fountain for longer than anyone thought you could, and then the flagstones come up to meet you. {flag(key_taken): When you get up, the key is gone from your pocket, and so is he.|When you get up he is gone, and the frost on the flagstones spells out a name: Kael's.}
> hide: Run, and take what he wants with you
  hint: Guile. Half the school is between you and the gate{flag(confronted_grey): , and he knows your face|}.
  challenge deceive expert -1 if flag(confronted_grey):
    win:
      guile +small
      say: You duck into the crowd and the crowd closes behind you; a dozen first-years suddenly need to cross the courtyard all at once. By the time he has walked through them, you're three corridors away {flag(star_key): with the key|with Kael}, and the bell for lessons is ringing.
    lose:
      if flag(star_key):
        unflag star_key
        flag key_taken
      else:
        gain grey_watching
      health -small
      mood -small
      say: He doesn't chase you. He simply arrives, at the end of the corridor, ahead of you. {flag(key_taken): He holds out his hand, and the key leaves your pocket on its own and goes to him.|"Tell him she's coming," he says, and leaves you shaking.}
> call: Shout for the headmistress
  hint: Sure. She'll want to know why he came for you.
  meet isolde
  rel isolde +small
  if flag(star_key):
    unflag star_key
    flag gave_star_key wardens_noticed
    say: She is there before you finish her name, and the courtyard thaws around her feet. He bows to her and goes. Then she holds out her own hand. "The key," she says, exactly as he did. "For safekeeping." You give it to her.
  else:
    rel kael -tiny
    say: She is there before you finish her name, and the courtyard thaws around her feet. He bows to her and goes. Kael, who heard the whole thing from a window, doesn't speak to you for a week: "You told her he was looking for me."

@event hs_key_recover
title: Getting It Back
type: menu
thread: hs_escalation
class: story
tone: tense
when: flag(key_taken) and not flag(star_key) and not flag(gave_star_key)
repeat: 2
weight: 18
art: key
tags: mystery hollowstar
# The star key taken (hs_grey_daylight): four ways back, three of them without a fight or a hard check, and "not yet",
# which brings this card back after its two-month cooldown (repeat: 2) (decision 2026-10-26: losing the key is harsh but never final).
scene: A narrow upstairs corridor of a village inn at night, a door with frost on its handle, a student with a candle hesitating outside it.
text: The man in grey has the star key, and by now the whole academy knows it. He has taken the top room at the Gilded Newt, and the landlord says he never seems to sleep. The headmistress has said nothing to you. Kael hasn't stopped saying things. There are ways to get it back, and none of them involve asking him nicely.
> isolde: Go to the headmistress
  hint: She'll get it back, and keep it until the night.
  when: flag(wardens_noticed) or flag(sided_wardens) or flag(warden_trial) or rel(isolde) >= 15
  unflag key_taken
  flag gave_star_key
  rel isolde +small
  mood -small
  say: She listens without a word, then puts on her coat. In the morning the key is on her desk, and there is frost on her sleeve up to the elbow. "He was polite about it," she says. "They always are." She doesn't give it back to you.
> steal: Steal it back from the Newt
  hint: Guile. He never seems to sleep.
  challenge deceive expert:
    win:
      unflag key_taken
      flag star_key
      find star_key
      say: He is sitting up in the dark with his eyes open, and he doesn't see you. The key is on the windowsill, in a dish of snow. You take it, and back out, and don't breathe until you're on the road.
    lose:
      health -small
      mood -small
      say: The landing creaks. He says "Good evening" through the closed door, and the cold comes under it like water. You run, and slip on the stairs, and get back to the castle with a sprained wrist and nothing else.
> family: Ask a Dumont where he'd keep it
  hint: Charm. Kael or Ilse know how the families hide things.
  when: flag(kael_ally) or flag(ilse_saved)
  challenge negotiate adept likely:
    win:
      unflag key_taken
      flag star_key
      find star_key
      say: "Snow," says {flag(ilse_saved): Ilse|Kael}, at once. "He'll keep it in snow, so it can't call to anyone." It's on his windowsill, in a dish of it. The Dumont who told you stands lookout in the lane while you climb, and doesn't say a word on the way home.
    lose:
      mood -small
      say: "I don't know," {flag(ilse_saved): Ilse|Kael} says, too quickly, and won't look at you. Whatever the families do with what they take, it isn't something they want to tell you. Not yet.
> wand: Let Edmund's wand find it
  hint: Arcana. The wand hums near anything the founders made.
  when: has_item(edmunds_silver_wand)
  challenge spell adept likely:
    win:
      unflag key_taken
      flag star_key
      find star_key
      mana -small
      say: The silver wand drags at your hand like a dog on a lead, all the way to the Newt and up the back stairs, and goes quiet beside a dish of snow on a windowsill. The man in grey is out. The key is not.
    lose:
      mana -small
      say: The wand hums, and wavers, and points at the lake every time. Wherever he's keeping it, it's near the water, and you can't follow it there. Not tonight.
> wait: Not yet
  hint: It'll keep. He will too.
  mood -tiny
  say: You leave it for now. Every night you can feel it from across the village, cold, the way you feel a draught from a door left open.
